# Secrets
.env

# Your preferences — language, size ceilings, taste. Personal, so it must not
# collide with an upstream pull. The tracked template is PREFS.example.md.
PREFS.md
# Contents are secret (emby_api_key) and personal: a watchlist is a record of
# what somebody watches, which is theirs and does not belong in a public
# repository. Only the template is tracked. Needs the glob rather than a bare
# "sync-state/": git will not descend into an excluded directory to un-exclude
# a file inside it.
sync-state/*
!sync-state/watchlist.example.txt

# Runtime state / generated
emby/
prowlarr/
library/
rclone/

# The dubbing workspace: a venv, several GB of model weights, downloaded
# episodes, stems and generated audio. All of it is rebuildable from
# scripts/dub_*.py, and none of it belongs in git. Anchored, because unanchored
# it excludes every directory named dub at any depth — .agents/skills/dub/
# among them, which is the tracked source of a skill.
/dub/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Project skills and the model pin ship with the repo; everything else under
# .claude/ is local agent state. The un-ignore of the directory has to come
# first — git will not descend into an excluded directory to re-include a file
# inside it — and it overrides a global core.excludesFile rule, which is where
# a personal ".claude/" usually lives.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
